architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:7:Source-control handling was path-scoped because the initial full MCP `git_status` response exceeded its output buffer. The bounded status captured in `pre-scope-evidence.stdout` shows this cycle directory as new/untracked and adjacent untracked evidence files under `architecture-audit/cycle-022-wave-plan-extension/`. Those adjacent files were not inspected beyond the assigned plan-extension note and were not reverted, reformatted, incorporated, or used as source authority. This task's intended changes are limited to:
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:24:- `frontend/src/application/world/initializeWorld.ts` only where initialization command ownership must be represented by the runtime/session boundary
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:25:- `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts` only as the concrete adapter target
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:35:`createAppShellRuntime` imports and constructs the concrete runtime objects directly: `CommandStack` and `World` are imported at `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellRuntime.ts:2-3` and instantiated at `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellRuntime.ts:17-18`. The same function owns all app-shell state refs, wires `ActivePlaneUseCases`, `SelectionDeletionCommandService`, `SelectionUseCases`, `AutoSaveUseCases`, `ProjectSessionUseCases`, and `KeyboardShortcutRouter`, then returns raw `world` and `commandStack` alongside UI state/actions (`frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellRuntime.ts:38-76`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellRuntime.ts:99-136`).
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:41:`AppShellPorts` imports `CommandStack`, `World`, and `ProjectData` solely to define app-shell persistence signatures (`frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellPorts.ts:2-5`). `ProjectSessionPersistencePort` exposes:
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:43:- `snapshotCurrentSession(deps: { commandStack: CommandStack; world: World; projectName: string }): ProjectData` at `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellPorts.ts:25-26`
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:45:- `restoreSession(data: ProjectData, deps: { world: World; commandStack: CommandStack }): void` at `frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellPorts.ts:28`
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:47:This leaks both concrete runtime kernel types and the concrete `ProjectService` DTO into app-shell port definitions.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:51:`ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter` imports concrete `CommandStack`, `World`, and `ProjectService`/`ProjectData` (`frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter.ts:1-4`). Its methods call `ProjectService.serializeCommands` with `commandStack`, `world.peekNextId()`, and project name (`frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter.ts:7-8`), validate via `ProjectService.validateProjectData` (`frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter.ts:11-12`), and restore via `ProjectService.deserializeCommands(data, world, commandStack)` (`frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter.ts:15-16`).
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:53:The adapter is the right place for `ProjectService` and concrete persistence DTO knowledge; the problem is that the adapter's shape is currently exported back into app-shell use cases.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:57:`ProjectSessionUseCases` imports `CommandStack`, `World`, `initializeWorld`, and `ProjectData` (`frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionUseCases.ts:1-7`). Its constructor receives raw `world` and `commandStack` (`frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionUseCases.ts:11-24`). It calls `initializeWorld(this.deps.world, this.deps.commandStack)` during no-Drive startup and fallback paths (`frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionUseCases.ts:31`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionUseCases.ts:50`), clears world and command history directly on sign-out/create/new (`frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionUseCases.ts:88-91`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionUseCases.ts:98-101`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionUseCases.ts:143-145`), snapshots by passing raw objects into `ports.persistence.snapshotCurrentSession` (`frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionUseCases.ts:101-105`), restores by passing raw objects into `ports.persistence.restoreSession` (`frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionUseCases.ts:122-126`), conditionally initializes after restore if no projection planes exist (`frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionUseCases.ts:127`), and marks the world dirty after opening (`frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionUseCases.ts:128`).
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:63:`AutoSaveUseCases` imports `CommandStack`, `World`, and the persistence port (`frontend/src/application/appShell/AutoSaveUseCases.ts:1-5`). It receives raw `world`/`commandStack` (`frontend/src/application/appShell/AutoSaveUseCases.ts:14-27`), polls `world.getVersion()` to schedule saves (`frontend/src/application/appShell/AutoSaveUseCases.ts:33-41`), and snapshots by passing raw objects to persistence in both the normal save path and missing-remote-file recovery path (`frontend/src/application/appShell/AutoSaveUseCases.ts:56-60`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/AutoSaveUseCases.ts:91-95`).
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:69:`initializeWorld` imports `Command`, `CommandStack`, initialization factory/process-tree operations, and `World` (`frontend/src/application/world/initializeWorld.ts:1-7`). It returns early if projection planes exist (`frontend/src/application/world/initializeWorld.ts:19-20`), creates an initialization command (`frontend/src/application/world/initializeWorld.ts:22`), adds process-tree and world-initialization operations (`frontend/src/application/world/initializeWorld.ts:24-30`), commits and pushes to command history (`frontend/src/application/world/initializeWorld.ts:33-34`), and marks the world dirty (`frontend/src/application/world/initializeWorld.ts:35`).
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:71:Wave 022 should not redesign initialization semantics, but startup/new/open fallback should call this behavior through the selected runtime-session owner rather than through an implicit helper that requires raw `World` and `CommandStack` everywhere.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:73:### `ProjectService` remains command-stream persistence and should stay adapter-private
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:75:`ProjectService` imports `World`, `CommandStack`, `Command`, operation descriptors, and `OperationRegistry` (`frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:5-9`). It serializes committed command snapshots plus `nextElementId` into schema `6.0.0` (`frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:11-41`), deserializes by clearing `commandStack`, restoring `nextElementId`, replaying operation descriptors into `world`, restoring committed commands, and fixing active-plane fallback (`frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:45-74`), and validates the current schema and operation descriptor shapes (`frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:80-136`).
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:81:`SelectionDeletionCommandService` owns command construction for the selection/delete slice: it stores concrete `World` and `CommandStack` privately (`frontend/src/application/selectionDeletion/SelectionDeletionCommandService.ts:20-29`) and executes by creating a command, delegating cascade deletion, committing, and pushing (`frontend/src/application/selectionDeletion/SelectionDeletionCommandService.ts:31-39`). `AppShellRuntime` wires it with the current runtime objects (`frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellRuntime.ts:40`).
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:91:3. Redefine `ProjectSessionPersistencePort` so app-shell use cases do not mention concrete `World`, `CommandStack`, or `ProjectData`.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:92:4. Keep `ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter` as the only app-shell bridge to `ProjectService` and current command-stream DTOs.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:93:5. Keep `ProjectService`, `OperationRegistry`, command descriptors, schema constants, Drive/auth internals, canvas/tool/process-history/toolbar command producers, rendering, backend, docs/specs, and package/tooling out of scope.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:101:- App-shell persistence and autosave still pass raw `World`/`CommandStack` pairs to persistence (`AppShellPorts.ts:25-28`, `ProjectSessionUseCases.ts:101-126`, `AutoSaveUseCases.ts:56-60`, `AutoSaveUseCases.ts:91-95`).
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:102:- `ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter` is already the only app-shell module directly importing `ProjectService` in the scoped files (`ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter.ts:3`).
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:103:- Initialization remains command-backed and touches history (`initializeWorld.ts:22-35`), so any session boundary must cover it explicitly.
