architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:129:- Changing `ProjectService` schema version, descriptor shape, replay algorithm, operation registry ownership, command snapshot format, or command-stack restore semantics.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:135:## Validation requirements for the eventual implementation
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:139:1. Pre-edit scoped git status/diff and static scans for app-shell imports/signatures exposing `World`, `CommandStack`, `ProjectData`, and `ProjectService`.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:141:3. Focused architecture/static boundary tests proving app-shell use-case ports no longer expose raw `World`/`CommandStack` persistence signatures and `ProjectService` remains adapter-private.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/scope-check.md:150:Proceed to `cycle-022-review-round-01` for review of this scope check plus the direct and restructure proposals. Do not implement before review convergence and a Cycle 022 decision artifact are recorded.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:5:Implement Wave 022 by introducing a small app-shell runtime-session boundary that owns the current `World` and `CommandStack` pair plus lifecycle operations that currently leak through app-shell use cases: initialize default world, clear session, snapshot current session, restore loaded project data, mark dirty after restore, observe version for autosave, and expose only the raw objects needed by already-reviewed consumers such as active-plane, keyboard undo/redo, canvas integration, and `SelectionDeletionCommandService` wiring.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:7:The direct path keeps the current `ProjectService` command-stream persistence implementation intact and moves its `ProjectData`/`World`/`CommandStack` knowledge behind adapter-private methods. It does not redesign command descriptors, schema/replay, Drive/auth, backend, rendering, or leaf command producers.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:18:  - Replace `ProjectSessionPersistencePort` raw-pair signatures with session-oriented methods that do not import `World`, `CommandStack`, or `ProjectData` in this port module.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:19:  - Introduce small DTO/opaque aliases if needed, such as `SerializedProjectSession` as `object`/`unknown` at the Drive boundary, without leaking `ProjectService.ProjectData` into use cases.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:21:  - Own `world: World` and `commandStack: CommandStack` privately or semi-privately.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:22:  - Provide explicit methods: `initializeDefaultWorldIfNeeded()`, `resetToEmptyInitializedWorld()`, `clear()`, `restoreProject(data)`, `snapshot(projectName)`, `getVersion()`, `markDirtyAfterRestore()` if needed, and narrow accessors for existing consumers that still legitimately need concrete objects in this wave.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:23:  - Delegate initialization to `initializeWorld(world, commandStack)` rather than changing initialization command semantics.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:25:  - Become adapter-private bridge from the session snapshot/restore request to `ProjectService.serializeCommands`, `ProjectService.validateProjectData`, and `ProjectService.deserializeCommands`.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:26:  - Continue importing `World`, `CommandStack`, and `ProjectData` only here or in the runtime-session owner if implementation chooses session-owned persistence delegation.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:28:  - Remove constructor dependencies on raw `World`, `CommandStack`, `initializeWorld`, and `ProjectData`.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:31:  - Remove constructor dependencies on raw `World` and `CommandStack`.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:33:- `frontend/src/application/world/initializeWorld.ts`
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:44:  - Add/replace static assertions: `AppShellPorts.ts` must not import `CommandStack`, `World`, or `ProjectData`; `ProjectSessionUseCases.ts` and `AutoSaveUseCases.ts` must not import `CommandStack`, `World`, `ProjectData`, or `initializeWorld`; `ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter.ts` remains the allowed `ProjectService` import.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:48:## Files/tests/docs/fixtures to DELETE
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:50:- Delete `ProjectSessionPersistencePort.snapshotCurrentSession(deps: { commandStack: CommandStack; world: World; projectName: string }): ProjectData`.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:51:- Delete `ProjectSessionPersistencePort.restoreSession(data: ProjectData, deps: { world: World; commandStack: CommandStack }): void`.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:52:- Delete app-shell port imports of `CommandStack`, `World`, and `ProjectData` once the new port shape is in place.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:53:- Delete direct `ProjectSessionUseCases` imports/dependencies on `CommandStack`, `World`, `ProjectData`, and `initializeWorld` where replaced by session methods.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:54:- Delete direct `AutoSaveUseCases` imports/dependencies on `CommandStack` and `World` where replaced by session methods.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:60:## Expected behavior change
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:64:Startup without Drive, startup with last project, create project, open project, new project, sign-out, autosave save/update, missing-remote-file recovery, selection deletion, undo/redo, active-plane setup, and save-status transitions should remain equivalent. Internal architecture changes: app-shell project/session use cases stop passing raw `World`/`CommandStack` pairs and stop importing concrete persistence DTOs.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:66:## No-backcompat rationale
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:70:## Validation plan
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:74:1. Pre-edit scoped `git status`/`git diff --stat` for touched paths and static scans for `World`, `CommandStack`, `ProjectData`, `ProjectService`, `snapshotCurrentSession`, `restoreSession`, and `initializeWorld` in app-shell files.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:80:   - `AppShellPorts.ts` no longer imports `World`, `CommandStack`, or `ProjectData`.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:82:   - `ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter.ts` remains the only app-shell `ProjectService` import.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:89:## Risks and mitigations
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:91:- **Risk: runtime session becomes a god object.** Mitigation: restrict it to runtime state ownership, initialization, snapshot/restore, clear/reset, version observation, and narrow raw-object accessors for existing consumers. Do not move leaf command construction or UI state into it.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:92:- **Risk: accidental schema/replay redesign.** Mitigation: keep `ProjectService` semantics unchanged and adapter-private. Stop for plan edit if descriptor/schema/replay changes become necessary.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:93:- **Risk: initialization history semantics shift.** Mitigation: preserve `initializeWorld` behavior and add focused assertions for startup/new/open fallback world initialization and command-stack counts where current tests support it.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:94:- **Risk: autosave timing regression.** Mitigation: keep scheduler/debounce behavior unchanged and update fake-scheduler tests around session version/snapshot methods.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:95:- **Risk: raw accessors undermine the boundary.** Mitigation: name them as explicit transitional adapter accessors for still-in-scope consumers and prohibit app-shell persistence/use-case ports from accepting the pair.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:97:## Stop conditions for broader redesign
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-direct.md:101:- Modifying `ProjectService` schema version, command snapshots, operation descriptors, replay algorithm, or `OperationRegistry`.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:5:This alternative asks whether the right fix is one conceptual layer higher than the direct proposal. Instead of adding only a small app-shell runtime-session wrapper, introduce an application-level session kernel boundary that becomes the composition root for runtime state, session lifecycle, persistence translation, and command-history exposure. App-shell use cases consume kernel ports (`SessionLifecyclePort`, `SessionPersistencePort`, `SessionHistoryPort`, `SessionReadPort`) rather than a single concrete `World`/`CommandStack` wrapper.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:7:The restructure path is appropriate only if review concludes the app-shell is already accumulating multiple runtime responsibilities that the direct session wrapper would centralize too weakly: project lifecycle, autosave, keyboard undo/redo, active-plane observation, selection-delete command service wiring, and future leaf command producers. It still must not redesign `ProjectService` schema/replay, command descriptors, backend, rendering, or leaf command producers inside Wave 022.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:14:  - `ApplicationSessionKernel.ts` or `RuntimeSessionKernel.ts`: owns `World`, `CommandStack`, initialization lifecycle, clear/reset, restore, snapshot, version, active-plane fallback/dirty marking.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:26:  - Remove `CommandStack`, `World`, and `ProjectData` imports from app-shell port contracts.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:33:  - Optional and bounded: consume `SessionHistoryPort` for undo/redo instead of direct `CommandStack`, only if review accepts this as necessary to make the kernel coherent. If this starts migrating command execution semantics, stop.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:37:  - Either move/rename under `sessionKernel` or leave as adapter-private bridge; in both cases it remains the only `ProjectService` bridge in the app-shell/session area.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:38:- `frontend/src/application/world/initializeWorld.ts`
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:40:- `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts`
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:46:- Update app-shell tests to mock kernel ports rather than concrete `World`/`CommandStack` pairs.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:47:- Update architecture boundary tests to enforce no app-shell port/use-case imports of `World`, `CommandStack`, `ProjectData`, or `ProjectService`, except for explicitly allowed composition and adapter files.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:49:## Files/tests/docs/fixtures to DELETE
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:52:- Delete app-shell use-case constructor fields for raw `World`/`CommandStack` where replaced by kernel ports.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:60:## Expected behavior change
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:64:## No-backcompat rationale
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:68:## Validation plan
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:75:   - app-shell ports/use cases do not import `World`, `CommandStack`, `ProjectData`, or `ProjectService`.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:76:   - `ProjectService` is imported only by the kernel/app-shell persistence adapter.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:84:## Risks and mitigations
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:86:- **Risk: over-abstracting into an application-kernel platform.** Mitigation: split only the ports needed by current app-shell/session flows; no event bus, service locator, generic command executor, or broad module migration.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:87:- **Risk: scope creep into keyboard/active-plane/selection.** Mitigation: touch those consumers only where the kernel must expose current world/history access clearly. Leave leaf command producers and rendering for later waves.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:88:- **Risk: adapter relocation churn without architectural payoff.** Mitigation: relocate `ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter` only if it makes `ProjectService` ownership clearer; otherwise keep it in app-shell and enforce adapter-private imports.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:89:- **Risk: persistence redesign sneaks in.** Mitigation: keep `ProjectService` schema/replay and command descriptors unchanged. Stop if current API cannot be hidden without changing those internals.
architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:90:- **Risk: more files changed than one cycle should handle.** Mitigation: prefer the direct proposal unless review finds direct wrapper would be an immediate god-object or would require follow-up churn in the next wave.
